# Reports written into the tree while testing. One of these held an AWS access
# key that had been pasted into a terminal, which a scan then found sitting in
# the working directory: untracked, but one `git add -A` from being committed.
/viewer/*.json
/topgent-report.json
/*.cdx.json

# The fuzzer's own corpus. libFuzzer writes tens of thousands of inputs it
# found interesting, which is 61 MB of machine-generated noise nobody reads.
# The inputs worth keeping are the ones that found a bug, and those are kept
# deliberately under fuzz/seeds with a test beside them.
/fuzz/corpus/
